The error message "Uncaught TypeError: Cannot add property value, object is not extensible" indicates that the code is attempting to add a property to an object that has been made non-extensible. This typically happens when `Object.preventExtensions()`, `Object.seal()`, or `Object.freeze()` has been applied to an object, preventing new properties from being added.

In the provided code snippet, the issue likely arises in the `updateCache` method of the `CascaderSelect` component. The method modifies the `this._v2n` and `this._p2n` objects by adding properties to them. If these objects are non-extensible, this will cause the error.

